r","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Darryl F. Zanuck","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"The award was named for and first given to the director Cecil B. DeMille himself."},{"id":"q6","question":"Since 1951, the Globes have split their top film categories into Drama and which other genre?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Musical or Comedy","is_correct":true},{"id":"b","text":"Action","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"Horror","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Documentary","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Since 1951 the Globes crown separate winners for Drama and for Musical or Comedy."},{"id":"q7","question":"At which Beverly Hills hotel has the Golden Globes ceremony long been held?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The Beverly Wilshire","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"The Beverly Hilton","is_correct":true},{"id":"c","text":"The Peninsula","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"The Bel-Air","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"The Beverly Hilton has hosted the Globes since 1961."},{"id":"q8","question":"The Carol Burnett Award, established in 2019, honours lifetime achievement in which field?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Television","is_correct":true},{"id":"b","text":"Film direction","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"Comedy writing","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Journalism","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"The Burnett Award is the TV counterpart of the film-focused DeMille Award; Carol Burnett was its first recipient."}]'::jsonb,
